; game.mant -- the two programs of Mantissa Dodge, as documentation.
;
; python3 gpu/python/make_game.py builds these (see its PROGRAM strings for
; the authoritative text, with the data addresses computed from the assembled
; size); gpu/python/run_game.py drives them, a frame at a time:
;
;     1. patch the frame number, the player's x, alive and score into the
;        referee machine and run it: it advances the obstacles (their z is a
;        MOD of the frame number, so no state is needed), tests the player
;        against each lane with ABS, LT and MUL-as-AND, freezes the score on
;        a hit, and writes the obstacle positions for the pixel machines;
;     2. patch the player and the obstacles into every pixel machine and run
;        them: each one casts its own ray (SQRT to normalise), finds the
;        checkerboard floor (CHOP, MOD) and the nearest of four spheres (the
;        quadratic formula), and stores the colour as one packed double,
;         r*65536 + g*256 + b
;        -- exact in every format, and just under the float wall;
;     3. the console decodes the colours into a picture and carries alive and
;        score to the next frame.
;
; The pixel program's blocks, in order:
;
; ; the ray
;         LDI.F  f1, {col}
;         LD.D   d0, [f1]
;         ...                  col and row become u, v, then
;         SQRT.D d5, d5        the length of (u, v, 1)
;         DIV.D  d6, d0, d5    rd x
;         DIV.D  d7, d1, d5    rd y
;         DIV.D  d8, d4, d5    rd z
; ; the floor, y = -1, is a candidate if the ray points down
;         BLT.D  d7, d11, floor_yes
; ; its colour: (floor(hx) + floor(hz)) mod 2 picks light or dark
;         CHOP.D d11, d13
;         CHOP.D d0, d0
;         MOD.D  d11, d11, d0
; ; each ball: the quadratic formula
;         SUB.D  d2, d2, d1    disc = b*b - cc
;         SQRT.D d2, d2
;         SUB.D  d3, d3, d2    t = -b - sqrt(disc)
;         BLE.D  d3, d9, nearer
; ; and the winner writes the packed colour and halts
;         ST.D   [f5], d10
;         HALT
;
; Everything a picture needs, out of sign, exponent and significand.
